# The same {B/G/P} shard paid with its other colour instead --
# ChoosePayHybridPhyrexian answering green -- proving the choice is not
# fixed to the first-named colour the way a careless implementation reading
# only s.Colors()'s first bit might get away with against color1 alone.
# Main phase of turn 1, so the payment is made at a priority (L2 S19); the
# lands are tapped there, since a pool loaded by setup.state empties as the
# steps pass (CR 500.4).
startturn human
advance 3
tapformana human 1 G
queue payhybridphyrexian G
paymanacost human B/G/P
